# apps/cyrus-site: cyrus.my static landing

Source: `src/` (imported from `/root/agent-notes/cyrus-designs/v7-landing`, the page live on cyrus.my since 2026-10-11).
No build step beyond a copy + manifest. `./publish.sh check|build|publish [--go]|rollback|list|import <dir>`; publishing is
a dry run unless `--go` and is owner/parent-gated. Details: `docs/CYRUS-PLATFORM.md` (section "Site").

## Off demo mode (2026-10-14)

The prompt box is a real form (`GET /sign-in?prompt=...`); after sign-in or sign-up the words arrive pre-filled in `/new`.
The hero animation is an illustration (it types into the placeholder, labelled as such). Plan numbers and the launch
state come from `GET /api/cyrus/launch` at view time; without it the page keeps its private-beta wording and shows no
number. Featured mods are build-time and optional: `CYRUS_SITE_FEATURED_JSON=https://nxeon.cloud/api/cyrus/featured`
(404 until the mods launch flag is on = no section). No link on the page may point at nxeon.cloud
(`test/cyrus-site-links.test.ts`); Terms / Privacy are served on cyrus.my.

## The CTAs are real (2026-10-13)

"Sign in" and "Sign in with Nxeon" are plain anchors to `/sign-in`, the bottom "Get started" to `/sign-up`; the hero
"Get started" still focuses the prompt. The page works without JS and carries no `data-demo` stubs
(`test/cyrus-site-landing.test.ts` pins this).

**Publishing is the owner's step.** Merging the branch does not change cyrus.my: nginx serves the static release, so run
on the primary node, from the merged checkout:

    apps/cyrus-site/publish.sh check
    apps/cyrus-site/publish.sh publish          # dry run: shows what would go live
    apps/cyrus-site/publish.sh publish --go     # atomic swap; rollback: publish.sh rollback --go

`/sign-in` and `/sign-up` are served by the app on the Cyrus host (lib/cyrus/bridge/routing.ts), so nginx must pass them
through to the app (it already does for the studio and auth paths).
